IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ny-pit`

-- New York Tax Law Article 22 -- the resident individual taxpayer's questions, for tax years 2026 and 2027.
-- Every question calls the rules in ny-pit.l4; nothing is restated here. Plain inputs, one per fact the person can state.
-- Federal amounts (AGI, the federal earned income credit, the number of dependants) come from the person's federal
-- return; see the IRC encoding in subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986/.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Am I a New York resident`

@export Am I a New York resident individual for the tax year under Tax Law s 605(b)(1)?
GIVEN `I am domiciled in New York` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether New York is your domicile (your permanent home, the place you intend to return to) for the year
      `I keep a permanent place of abode in New York` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you maintain a permanent place to live in New York (owned, rented or otherwise kept for you) during the year
      `I keep a permanent place of abode outside New York` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you maintain a permanent place to live outside New York during the year
      `days I spent in New York` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days (or parts of days) in total you spent in New York in the tax year
      `I meet the 548-day foreign presence test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in some 548 consecutive days, you were in foreign countries for at least 450 days and you, your spouse and minor children were in New York no more than 90 days, with the matching limit on days in each part-year (s 605(b)(1)(A)(ii))
      `I am in active service in the US armed forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are on active service in the United States armed forces
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a New York resident` IF
    `is a resident individual` `I am domiciled in New York` `I keep a permanent place of abode in New York` `I keep a permanent place of abode outside New York` `days I spent in New York` `I meet the 548-day foreign presence test` `I am in active service in the US armed forces`

§ `Must I file, and by when`

@export What is my New York standard deduction under Tax Law s 614?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status, the same as on your federal return: single, married filing jointly, married filing separately, head of household, or surviving spouse
      `someone else can claim me as a dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another taxpayer can claim you as a dependant on their return
      `the cost-of-living increase to the standard deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The dollar increase to the s 614 amount under s 614(f) (the Department of Taxation and Finance's figure for your status, as printed in the return instructions; 0 if you want the unadjusted statutory amount)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my New York standard deduction` MEANS
    `the New York standard deduction` `my filing status` `someone else can claim me as a dependant` `the cost-of-living increase to the standard deduction`

@export Must I file a New York State resident income tax return under Tax Law s 651(a)(1)?
GIVEN `I am a New York resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a New York resident individual for the tax year (see the residence question)
      `I must file a federal return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are required to file a federal income tax return for the year
      `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income for the year, in US dollars
      `my New York additions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the New York additions to federal AGI under s 612(b) (for example interest on other states' bonds), in US dollars; 0 if none
      `my New York standard deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc Your New York standard deduction (see the standard deduction question), in US dollars
      `I received a lump sum distribution taxed under s 603` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received a lump-sum retirement distribution any part of which is subject to the separate New York tax under s 603
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I file a New York return` IF
    `a resident must file a return under s 651(a)(1)` `I am a New York resident` `I must file a federal return` `my federal adjusted gross income` `my New York additions` `my New York standard deduction` `I received a lump sum distribution taxed under s 603`

@export By what date must I file my New York return and pay the tax under Tax Law ss 651(a) and 652(a)?
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar tax year, for example 2026
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I file and pay` MEANS `the due date for the return and the tax` `the tax year`

@export If I elected to have the Tax Department compute my tax, by what date must I pay it under Tax Law s 652(b)?
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar tax year, for example 2026
      `the date of the notice and demand` IS A DATE @desc The date on which the Department issued its notice and demand for the tax it computed
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I pay a tax the Department computed` MEANS
    `the last day to pay a tax the commissioner computed` `the tax year` `the date of the notice and demand`

§ `My New York income`

@export How much may I subtract under Tax Law s 612(c)(3-a) for private pensions, annuities and IRA distributions?
GIVEN `I am at least 59 and a half` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had reached age 59 and a half when the payments were received
      `my private pensions and annuities` IS A NUMBER @desc Your periodic pension and annuity payments from a former employer or a deductible retirement plan, and IRA and Keogh distributions, included in your federal AGI, in US dollars (not New York or federal government pensions, and not a lump sum taxed under s 603)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my pension subtraction` MEANS
    `the s 612(c)(3-a) subtraction for one person` `I am at least 59 and a half` `my private pensions and annuities`

@export What is my New York adjusted gross income under Tax Law s 612?
GIVEN `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Federal adjusted gross income on your federal return (joint if you file jointly), in US dollars
      `my New York additions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the s 612(b) additions, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `government pensions in my federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc New York State or local government and US federal government pensions included in federal AGI (s 612(c)(3)), in US dollars
      `my private pension subtraction` IS A NUMBER @desc Your own s 612(c)(3-a) subtraction (see the pension question), in US dollars
      `my spouse's private pension subtraction` IS A NUMBER @desc On a joint return, your spouse's own s 612(c)(3-a) subtraction, in US dollars; 0 otherwise
      `taxable social security in my federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of your social security benefits included in federal AGI under IRC s 86, in US dollars
      `my other New York subtractions` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other s 612(c) subtractions (for example US savings bond interest), in US dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my New York AGI` MEANS
    `New York adjusted gross income` `my federal adjusted gross income` `my New York additions` `government pensions in my federal AGI` `my private pension subtraction` `my spouse's private pension subtraction` `taxable social security in my federal AGI` `my other New York subtractions`

@export What is my New York taxable income under Tax Law ss 611, 613 and 616?
GIVEN `my New York AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your New York adjusted gross income (see the New York AGI question), in US dollars
      `my New York standard deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc Your New York standard deduction (see the standard deduction question), in US dollars
      `I elect to itemize` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you elect the New York itemized deduction under s 615
      `my New York itemized deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc Your New York itemized deduction under s 615, in US dollars; 0 if you do not itemize
      `my number of dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependants you are entitled to claim under IRC s 151(c) (not counting yourself or your spouse)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my New York taxable income` MEANS
    `New York taxable income` `my New York AGI` (`the New York deduction` `my New York standard deduction` `I elect to itemize` `my New York itemized deduction`) (`the New York exemptions` `my number of dependants`)

§ `My New York tax`

@export How much New York income tax is imposed on my New York taxable income under Tax Law s 601, before credits?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, married filing jointly, married filing separately, head of household, or surviving spouse
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar tax year: 2026 or 2027 (other years are not covered)
      `my New York AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your New York adjusted gross income, in US dollars (over $100,000 is not covered)
      `my New York taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your New York taxable income (see the taxable income question), in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much New York tax before credits` MEANS
    `the s 601 tax` `my filing status` `the tax year` `my New York AGI` `my New York taxable income`

§ `My credits`

@export How much is my New York household credit under Tax Law s 606(b)?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status
      `someone else can claim me as a dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another taxpayer can claim you as a dependant
      `my household's federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal AGI, plus your spouse's if you are married (even if you file separately), in US dollars
      `my federal exemptions` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of people on your federal return: you, your spouse if married, and your dependants
      `my New York tax before credits` IS A NUMBER @desc Your tax under s 601 (see the tax question), in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my household credit` MEANS
    `the household credit` `my filing status` `someone else can claim me as a dependant` `my household's federal AGI` `my federal exemptions` `my New York tax before credits`

@export Does this child count as a qualifying child for the Empire State child credit under Tax Law s 606(c-1)(1-a)(D)?
GIVEN `they are my child, sibling or stepsibling, or a descendant of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is your child (including stepchild, eligible foster child, or adopted or placed for adoption), brother, sister, stepbrother or stepsister, or a descendant of any of them
      `they lived with me for more than half the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child had the same principal home as you for more than half the tax year
      `their age at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age, in whole years, at the end of the tax year
      `they provided over half of their own support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child provided more than half of their own support for the year
      `they filed a joint return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child filed a joint return with a spouse for the year, other than only to claim a refund
      `they are a US citizen or national or have an ITIN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a US citizen or national, or has an individual taxpayer identification number from the IRS
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this child qualify for the Empire State child credit` IF
    `is a qualifying child under s 606(c-1)(1-a)(D)` `they are my child, sibling or stepsibling, or a descendant of one` `they lived with me for more than half the year` `their age at the end of the year` `they provided over half of their own support` `they filed a joint return` `they are a US citizen or national or have an ITIN`

@export How much is my Empire State child credit for tax year 2026 or 2027 under Tax Law s 606(c-1)(1-a)(B) and (C)?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status
      `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `qualifying children aged 0 to 3` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your qualifying children are aged three or younger
      `qualifying children aged 4 to 16` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your qualifying children are aged four to sixteen
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my Empire State child credit` MEANS
    `the Empire State child credit for 2026 or 2027` `my filing status` `my federal adjusted gross income` `qualifying children aged 0 to 3` `qualifying children aged 4 to 16`

@export How much is my New York earned income credit under Tax Law s 606(d)?
GIVEN `my federal earned income credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The earned income credit allowed on your federal return under IRC s 32, in US dollars
      `my household credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your New York household credit (see the household credit question), in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my New York earned income credit` MEANS
    `the New York earned income credit` `my federal earned income credit` `my household credit` FALSE

§ `What do I owe or get back`

@export As a New York resident, how much New York income tax do I owe after credits (a negative answer is a refund), for tax year 2026 or 2027?
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar tax year: 2026 or 2027
      `I am a New York resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a New York resident individual for the whole year (see the residence question)
      `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status, the same as on your federal return
      `someone else can claim me as a dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another taxpayer can claim you as a dependant
      `I received a lump sum distribution taxed under s 603` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received a lump-sum retirement distribution subject to the separate s 603 tax
      `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Federal AGI on your return (joint if you file jointly), in US dollars
      `my spouse's federal AGI on a separate return` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are married filing separately, your spouse's federal AGI, in US dollars; 0 otherwise
      `my New York additions` IS A NUMBER @desc s 612(b) additions, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `my New York subtractions` IS A NUMBER @desc All your s 612(c) subtractions together (government pensions, the pension subtraction, taxable social security, others), in US dollars
      `the cost-of-living increase to the standard deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 614(f) increase to the standard deduction for your status, in US dollars (0 for the unadjusted statutory amount)
      `I elect to itemize` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you elect the New York itemized deduction
      `my New York itemized deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc Your New York itemized deduction, in US dollars; 0 if you do not itemize
      `my number of dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependants you can claim (not yourself or your spouse)
      `qualifying children aged 0 to 3` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Empire State child credit qualifying children are aged three or younger
      `qualifying children aged 4 to 16` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Empire State child credit qualifying children are aged four to sixteen
      `my federal earned income credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal earned income credit on your return, in US dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much New York tax do I owe after credits` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am a New York resident`
    THEN `not covered` `only resident individuals are encoded; nonresident and part-year resident tax (s 601(e), Part III) is not`
    ELSE IF `I received a lump sum distribution taxed under s 603`
         THEN `not covered` `a lump sum distribution taxed under s 603 is not encoded`
         ELSE
             LET `standard deduction` MEANS `the New York standard deduction` `my filing status` `someone else can claim me as a dependant` `the cost-of-living increase to the standard deduction`
                 `NY AGI` MEANS `New York adjusted gross income` `my federal adjusted gross income` `my New York additions` 0 0 0 0 `my New York subtractions`
                 `taxable` MEANS `New York taxable income` `NY AGI` (`the New York deduction` `standard deduction` `I elect to itemize` `my New York itemized deduction`) (`the New York exemptions` `my number of dependants`)
                 `married` MEANS `my filing status` EQUALS `married filing jointly` OR `my filing status` EQUALS `married filing separately`
                 `exemptions on the federal return` MEANS (IF `married` THEN 2 ELSE 1) PLUS `my number of dependants`
                 `household income` MEANS `my federal adjusted gross income` PLUS `my spouse's federal AGI on a separate return`
             IN CONSIDER `the s 601 tax` `my filing status` `the tax year` `NY AGI` `taxable`
                WHEN `not covered` r THEN `not covered` r
                WHEN `answered` tax THEN
                    LET `household` MEANS `the household credit` `my filing status` `someone else can claim me as a dependant` `household income` `exemptions on the federal return` tax
                        `ESCC` MEANS `the Empire State child credit for 2026 or 2027` `my filing status` `my federal adjusted gross income` `qualifying children aged 0 to 3` `qualifying children aged 4 to 16`
                        `EIC` MEANS `the New York earned income credit` `my federal earned income credit` `household` FALSE
                    IN `answered` (`tax less credits` tax `household` `ESCC` `EIC`)
